  "jobTitle": "Senior Systems Software Engineer",
  "summary": "Mr. Nguyen has 25 years of experience including 16 years of relevant experience for the United States Air Force (USAF), Defense Information Systems Agency (DISA), U.S. Customs Service, and MCI WorldCom. For thirteen years, he has served as Senior Systems Software Engineer for the USAF Deliberate and Crisis Action Planning and Execution System (DCAPES). He provides Oracle 11g operational database support for multiple DCAPES applications that are replicated among four USAF commands with two thousand users worldwide. Mr. Nguyen provides technical leadership and guidance to a team of site Oracle database administrators (DBAs) and systems administrators (SAs) and coordinates database and applications monitoring, performance tuning, troubleshooting, and software maintenance. Using his expertise in database administration and data management, he resolves highly complex Oracle database and DCAPES applications issues such as timely fixing database corruption, database recovery, DCAPES distributed database transaction, JOPES JDNETS/JSUB and DCAPES web services, WebLogic server, and database performance tuning. He regularly provides valuable recommendations and assistance to Global Command and Control System-Air Force Technical Support Center (TSC) and field engineers for systems software installation, configuration, and deployment to ensure high availability and performance for DCAPES applications on operational and test systems. He is an Oracle 11g Certified DBA Professional (OCP) and is certified in Security+. He holds a Masters degree in Software Engineering and a Graduate Certificate in Information Engineering from George Mason University.\n",
